[img]http://aeonoftime.com/linked/nexusmods/starfield/header_slok.png[/img]

SLOK is a lightweight Windows tool that keeps your Starfield [font=Courier New]Plugins.txt[/font] stable and prevents 
accidental load-order changes that can break saves.

[b]Table of Contents[/b]

[list]
[*]Why it exists
[*]What it does
[*]How to use[list][*]New playthrough[*]Loading a savegame[*]Adding new mods[*]Deleting mods[*]Replacing mods[/list]
[*]Limitations
[*]Vortex Installation
[*]Manual Installation
[*]More on GitHub
[/list]
[img]http://aeonoftime.com/linked/nexusmods/starfield/header_why_it_exists.png[/img]

Starfield depends on the exact order of mods listed in [font=Courier New]Plugins.txt[/font].  
If that order changes after you start a save, items, quests, or entire characters can break.  
Unfortunately, Starfield, Mod managers and tools like LOOT can cause the file to be reordered.

SLOK helps you to stop that from happening.

[img]http://aeonoftime.com/linked/nexusmods/starfield/header_what_it_does.png[/img]

[list]
[*]Saves a reference copy of a known-good [font=Courier New]Plugins.txt[/font]
[*]Detects when the file changes
[*]Visualizes changes with editing capabilities
[*]Restores the correct order with one click
[*]Supports profiles for multiple load orders
[*]Maintains a version history with rollback support
[*]Launches the game (uses SFSE if present)
[/list]
[img]http://aeonoftime.com/linked/nexusmods/starfield/header_how_to_use.png[/img]

[size=2][b]New Playthrough[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Set up your load order in Starfield or your mod manager.
[*]Run SLOK, which automatically creates a copy as sorting reference.
[*]Optional: Create a profile for the playthrough.
[*]Run Starfield.
[*]Keep an eye on SLOK for any changes to [font=Courier New]Plugins.txt[/font].
[/list]

If anyone changes the `Plugins.txt file, SLOK will detect them, and you can
use the changes window to see what exactly changed and restore the correct order.

[size=2][b]Loading a savegame[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Run SLOK.
[*]Run Starfield.
[*]Before confirming the savegame to load, check SLOK for any changes.
[*]Reorder mods if needed to match the reference.
[*]Load your savegame safely.
[/list]

For example, Starfield can update the load order after clicking "Continue" on the
main menu, and before you confirm loading. Resetting the load order before you 
click "Confirm" ensures your save stays stable.

[size=2][b]Adding new mods[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install mods using your mod manager.
[*]Sort the load order as desired, run LOOT...
[*]Run SLOK.
[*]Sort mods.
[*]New mods will be appended at the end.
[*]Update the reference file to accept the added mods.
[/list]

Adding mods typically works without issues. 

One problematic use case is when want to add a mod that should be loaded before 
or after another mod in your load order. This will change your load order, which
can break your save. Only testing will tell if it works.

[size=2][b]Deleting mods[/b][/size]

Avoid deleting any mods mid-playthrough if at all possible. It will change your
load order, and possibly break your save. One possible workaround is to replace
the deleted mod with a new mod to avoid the load order shift (see "Replacing mods").

If really you must delete mods, follow these steps:

[list=1]
[*]Delete the target mods.
[*]Run SLOK.
[*]Sort mods.
[*]Update the reference file to accept the deleted mods.
[/list]
NOTE: You will probably see a lot of changes in the load order even after sorting: 
Those are all the mods that shifted due to the deletion.

[size=2][b]Replacing mods[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Delete the target mod, and add the replacement mod.
[*]Run SLOK.
[*]Sort mods.
[*]Right-click the deleted mod.
[*]Choose "Replace with...".
[*]Choose the target mod.
[*]Update the reference file to accept the replacements.
[/list]
[img]http://aeonoftime.com/linked/nexusmods/starfield/header_limitations.png[/img]

The tool is made primarily to sort mods according to the reference list. It can handle some
cases like removed, replaced or inserted mods, but only to a certain extent. Combining many
different changes, for example, can possibly not be displayed in a meaningful way.

You can still update the reference file with the changes you made, but it's really up to you
to know what you are doing.                                                                             

[img]http://aeonoftime.com/linked/nexusmods/starfield/header_vortex_installation.png[/img]

[list=1]
[*]Download the app via Vortex like you would any mod. 
[*]Once downloaded, set it to "Disabled" (no need to deploy it, but you can if you prefer).
[*]Right-click the mod in Vortex, and choose "Open in File Manager".
[*]Run the EXE to start the app.
[/list]
> TIP: You can also create a shortcut in your Windows taskbar or in Vortex for easier access.

[img]http://aeonoftime.com/linked/nexusmods/starfield/header_manual_installation.png[/img]

[list=1]
[*]Download the ZIP from the files section.
[*]Extract it anywhere you like. 
[*]Run the EXE, no installation required.
[/list]
> NOTE: If you prefer an installer, you can find one in the [url=https://github.com/Mistralys/starfield-load-order-manager/releases]GitHub Releases page[/url].

[img]http://aeonoftime.com/linked/nexusmods/starfield/header_more_on_github.png[/img]

The tool is open source and available on GitHub:

[url=https://github.com/Mistralys/starfield-load-order-manager]starfield-load-order-manager[/url]

Feel free to report issues there or contribute!
